{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFive Python store-test modules contain 43 audited prose blocks with incident history, duplicated rationale, obvious narration, or ornamental banners. Scope was revalidated against `origin/main@d6669496cae4`; the newly expanded Windows exclusive-leg suite accounts for 21 blocks.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only the 43 allowlisted true leading docstrings and contiguous full-line comment blocks. Parse immutable before/final blobs with `type_comments=True`; on comparison copies remove only allowlisted leading `Expr(Constant(str))` nodes from `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, and `AsyncFunctionDef`, normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`, and require normalized AST equality.\n\nTokenize comments by enclosing symbol and unchanged code anchor. Reject changes to inline comments, directives, non-allowlisted blocks, runtime strings, regexes, marker text, imports, decorators, annotations, subprocess arguments, assertions, and test data. Adjacent blank-line normalization is allowed only around an edited block.\n\n## Stable block allowlist\n- `test_git_outcome.py` — `D:<module>` and docstrings of `test_policy_decline_wins_over_a_bare_rejected`, `test_invalid_object_is_its_own_kind_and_keeps_the_rebuild_recovery`, and `test_a_policy_decline_is_subtracted_from_both_retriable_predicates` (4).\n- `test_merge_recovery.py` — `D:<module>` (1).\n- `test_stamped_lock.py` — `D:<module>`; comments before `test_acquire_stamps_the_file_and_release_removes_it`, `test_release_unlinks_even_when_close_fails`, `_MARKER_RE`, and `_tracker`; and docstrings of `test_release_unlinks_even_when_close_fails`, `_acquire_offenders`, `test_the_stamped_lock_acquire_appears_only_in_its_owner`, and `test_every_worker_still_excludes_a_second_holder_and_releases` (9).\n- `test_store_paths.py` — `D:<module>`; comments before `_canonical_store`, `test_a_symlinked_worktree_view_derives_the_canonical_stores_sidecars`, `test_a_plain_tracker_is_its_own_canonical`, `_MARKER_RE`, and `test_every_real_sidecar_helper_lands_in_the_one_canonical_rebar`; and docstrings of `test_the_tracker_sibling_rebar_derivation_appears_only_in_paths` and `test_every_real_sidecar_helper_lands_in_the_one_canonical_rebar` (8).\n- `test_windows_exclusive_leg.py` — `D:<module>`; full-line blocks opening “layer 1: no leg”, “Make the child interpreter”, “layer 2: the Windows leg”, “Reusable once released”, “the liveness probe”, and “layer 3: the real Windows primitive”; and docstrings of `test_no_leg_acquire_refuses_loudly_and_never_takes_the_mkdir_leg`, `test_no_leg_busy_probe_fails_open`, `test_no_leg_doctor_probe_reports_unknown`, `_windows_shaped_msvcrt`, `windows_leg`, `test_windows_leg_write_lock_round_trips`, `test_windows_leg_excludes_a_second_acquirer`, `test_windows_leg_exclusion_survives_the_mkdir_leg_being_removed`, `test_windows_leg_busy_probe_answers_truthfully`, `test_windows_leg_doctor_probe_answers_truthfully`, `test_pid_probe_never_signals_where_signal_zero_terminates`, `test_narrowed_pid_probe_does_not_reclaim_a_fresh_lock_without_proof`, `test_native_lock_is_visible_across_processes`, and `test_native_lock_dies_with_its_holder` (21).\n\n`D:<symbol>` means the true leading docstring owned by that qualified symbol. A comment block is the maximal contiguous full-line block identified by its enclosing symbol, opening words, and next unchanged executable anchor. No other prose is editable.\n\n## Preserved contracts and consumers\n- Git outcomes remain operation-sensitive; policy declines subtract from retriable predicates; invalid-object failures still trigger index rebuild.\n- Merge recovery retains tracked/untracked, common-dir, vanished-path, parser-refusal, convergence, and mandatory-reason fences.\n- Stamped locking retains release independence, bounded acquisition/reclamation, owner matching, mandatory-reason escape, and real-worker exclusion.\n- Store paths retain canonical symlink resolution, plain/unreadable degradation, frozen derivations, tracker-sibling uniqueness, and real-sidecar coverage.\n- Windows locking retains fail-loudly behavior with no exclusive leg; real kernel exclusion before mkdir reclamation; advisory/doctor degradation; POSIX-host simulation versus native-Windows proof; conservative PID liveness; and release-on-process-death.\n- Pytest and the reduced macOS compatibility lane execute these modules. `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` is the deterministic prose consumer. No runtime docstring reader was found.\n\nIn `test_windows_exclusive_leg.py`, preserve `_NO_LEG`, `_CHILD_HOLDS_THE_LOCK`, every embedded/inline comment inside runtime strings, the concise `_spawn_holder` docstring, the `pytest.skip` reason, and `# pragma: no cover` byte-for-byte. Preserve the three existing `type: ignore` directive-bearing lines in the other files and every other inline comment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Changes are limited to the 43 stable-ID prose blocks and adjacent blank lines; normalized-AST and token/comment comparisons pass for all five paths.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and preserves its listed constraint or consumer; history, duplication, obvious narration, and separator ornament are removed.\n- [ ] A non-author reviewer posts a leaf-linked TSV row per edited block: `stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session`.\n- [ ] All 43 rows cite immutable blobs and record `directives_exact=PASS`, `semantic-preservation=PASS`, and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing or failing rows block closure.\n- [ ] Exact changed paths, focused pytest, scoped Ruff, comment hygiene, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded allowlist-aware normalized-AST/comment/directive comparator, exact changed-path check, focused tests and Ruff, comment hygiene, path-scoped diff check, and no-timeout `make verify`. The independent TSV is authoritative for prose quality."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788623843660933001,"uuid":"23fa2814-2e9b-4dc8-a8f4-0ebdd6cfea29"}